  "answer_markdown": "After you describe the outcome you want in natural language in **Vibe Work**, the following happens [1][3][4]:\n\n1. **Vibe gathers context**: It collects relevant information from your prompt, attached files, connected tools (e.g., email, GitHub, Google Drive), or the web [1][3].\n\n2. **Vibe plans and acts**: It breaks the task into smaller, actionable steps and executes them sequentially. During execution, it shows progress in real time, including reasoning steps, tool calls (e.g., web searches), and results [1][3][4].\n\n3. **You review and steer**: Vibe displays a **todos panel** with live updates for each step, asks for **clarifying questions** when needed, and requests **approval before sensitive actions** (e.g., modifying files, accessing external apps, or making calendar changes) [1][3][4]. You can:\n   - Stop the task at any point using the black square button.\n   - Send follow-up messages to redirect or refine the task mid-execution.\n   - Inspect outputs and request revisions before finalizing.\n\n### How Vibe Keeps You in Control [1][3][4][5][6]:\n- **Approval before sensitive actions**: Vibe explicitly asks for confirmation before executing actions that affect your data, calendar, or external tools.\n- **Live progress tracking**: Every step is visible in real time, including tool calls and intermediate results.\n- **Editable and reusable outputs**: Results are inspectable, editable, and can be reused across sessions.\n- **Approval model**: For file changes (e.g., in **Vibe Code**), you can review each edit individually or approve in bulk (e.g., per file, directory, or globally) [5][6].\n- **Stop/redirect capability**: You can halt execution or guide Vibe with additional instructions during runtime.\n\nExample approval workflow in **Vibe Code** (CLI or VS Code extension):\n```\n# Preview of changes before applying:\nVibe Code shows:\n- Files to be created/modified.\n- Content of each file.\n- Confirmation prompt (e.g., `Enter` to approve, `N` to reject).\n```\n\nThis ensures transparency and control at every stage [5][6].",
