  "answer_markdown": "To build a real-time voice agent that transcribes live audio and replies with a cloned brand voice, you should combine the following Mistral models and expect the following constraints:\n\n### **Recommended Models**\n1. **Voxtral Realtime** (`voxtral-mini-transcribe-realtime-2602`) for live transcription with sub-200ms latency [1][3].\n2. **An LLM** (not specified in the sources, but required for reasoning and generating responses).\n3. **Voxtral TTS** (`voxtral-mini-tts-2603`) for voice cloning and speech generation with ~90ms processing latency [1][2][5].\n\n### **End-to-End Pipeline**\nThe workflow follows this sequence:\n1. **Live audio input** → **Voxtral Realtime** (transcribes with sub-200ms latency) [1][3].\n2. **Transcript** → **LLM** (processes and generates a response).\n3. **Response** → **Voxtral TTS** (generates speech with cloned brand voice, ~90ms processing latency) [1][2][5].\n\n### **Latency Constraints**\n- **Transcription latency**: Configurable down to **sub-200ms** for live audio [1][3].\n- **TTS processing latency**: **~90ms** for time-to-first-audio [2][5].\n- **End-to-end latency**: Depends on LLM inference time (not specified in sources) + TTS streaming (~0.8s for `pcm`, ~3s for `mp3`) [2].\n\n### **Voice Cloning Constraints**\n- **Sample requirement**: As short as **2–3 seconds** of audio to clone a voice [1][2][5].\n- **Voice preservation**: Captures tone, rhythm, and personality without needing prosody tags [1][2].\n- **Multilingual support**: Works across **9 languages** with cross-lingual cloning [1][2][5].\n\n### **Deployment Notes**\n- **Edge deployment**: Voxtral Realtime supports **on-premises or VPC deployment** with open weights (Apache 2.0) [1][3].\n- **Voice management**: Clone and reuse voices via the [Voices API](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/audio/text_to_speech/voices) [1][4].\n\n### **Example Code for Voice Cloning**\nTo create a reusable voice profile (e.g., for branding), use the following API call:\n\n```python\nimport base64\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom mistralai.client import Mistral\n\nclient = Mistral(api_key=\"your-api-key\")\nsample_audio_b64 = base64.b64encode(Path(\"brand_voice.mp3\").read_bytes()).decode()\n\nvoice = client.audio.voices.create(\n    name=\"brand-voice\",\n    sample_audio=sample_audio_b64,\n    sample_filename=\"brand_voice.mp3\",\n    languages=[\"en\"],\n    gender=\"female\",\n)\nprint(f\"Created voice: {voice.id}\")\n```\n\nThis voice can then be referenced by `voice_id` in TTS requests for consistent branding [4].",
