  "answer_markdown": "To enforce a size limit when loading files from an S3 bucket using `S3FileLoader`, you can use the `max_file_size` parameter. This parameter rejects files that exceed the specified size in bytes before loading them into memory. Here is how to do it:

```python
from mistralai.search.toolkit.plugins.storage.s3 import S3FileLoader

loader = S3FileLoader(
    bucket_name="my-bucket",
    region_name="us-east-1",
    max_file_size=50 * 1024 * 1024,  # 50 MiB
)
file = await loader.load_file("reports/example.pdf")
```

If a file exceeds the `max_file_size` limit, a `FileSizeLimitExceededException` will be raised [1].",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "Reject files larger than this many bytes"
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

