For the endpoint `POST /v1/chat/classifications`, the following fields in the `ChatClassificationRequest` body are required and their types are as follows [1]:

- **`model`** (string, required): ID of the model to use.
- **`input`** (ChatClassificationRequestInputs, required): Chat to classify, which can be one of the following:
  - **`InstructRequest`** (object, required):
    - **`messages`** (array of object, required): The chat messages to classify.

The `input` field can also be an array of `InstructRequest` objects.

### Example Structure
```json
{
  "model": "<model-id>",
  "input": {
    "messages": [
      {"role": "user", "content": "<message-content>"},
      {"role": "assistant", "content": "<message-content>"}
    ]
  }
}
```

or

```json
{
  "model": "<model-id>",
  "input": [
    {
      "messages": [
        {"role": "user", "content": "<message-content>"},
        {"role": "assistant", "content": "<message-content>"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "messages": [
        {"role": "user", "content": "<another-message>"}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

