message.content:
{
  "answer_markdown": "To fetch live data from a connected tool like **Gmail, Drive, or Notion** in Mistral's **Work chat**, you should use **Connectors** [3]. This feature allows Work to securely retrieve, analyze, and act on data from external tools without requiring you to switch between apps manually [3].\n\n### Key Differences from Web Search:\n- **Connectors** are designed for **direct integration with tools** (e.g., Gmail, Notion, Google Drive) to fetch real-time data from your accounts or workspaces [3].\n- **Web Search** and **Open URL** are used for **publicly available web content** (e.g., searching the internet or analyzing a specific webpage) [1].\n\n### How to Use Connectors:\n1. Ensure the tool (e.g., Gmail, Notion) is connected via the **Connectors** page in the sidebar [3].\n2. Enable the relevant Connector in the chat by clicking the `+` icon or typing `/`, then selecting `Tools` and choosing the Connector [3].\n3. Describe your task naturally (e.g., *“Summarize my unread emails from the legal team”*), and Work will fetch the data from the connected tool [3].\n\n### Example Use Cases:\n- Fetching emails from Gmail [3].\n- Retrieving documents from Google Drive [3].\n- Extracting content from Notion databases [3].\n\nFor **public web data**, use **Web Search** or **Open URL** instead [1].",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "Pick the option that fits your situation: ... Pull live data from a connected tool (Gmail, Drive, Notion...) | **[Connectors](https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/work/connectors)**"
