  "answer_markdown": "Yes, an agent can create a new version of a Skill in Mistral Studio. When you update a Skill (e.g., modifying its instructions or attached files), Studio automatically creates a new version after saving the changes. You must add version notes to explain the changes, such as `Adds liability cap checks` or `Updates the summary table format` [1].\n\nOlder versions remain available for review and rollback, ensuring continuity for existing workflows or agents using the Skill [1].\n\nRegarding Skills written from your editor (e.g., in Studio), they **will show up in Vibe Work** only if you explicitly publish them to Vibe. To do this:\n\n1. Open the Skill in Studio.\n2. Click **Publish to Vibe** on the Skill details page [1].\n\nOnce published, the Skill will appear in Vibe Work under either **Personal** (if private) or **Workspace** (if shared) and can be used by agents in Vibe [3].",
