  "answer_markdown": "To investigate who deleted conversations programmatically, an administrator should query the audit logs for the following details:\n\n1. **Activity and Event Type**:\n   - Look for the event type `le_chat.conversation.deleted` in the audit logs, as this records when a le Chat conversation is deleted [4].\n\n2. **Query Parameters to Narrow Results to a Specific Human User**:\n   - Use the `actor_type` parameter with the value `HUMAN` to filter for actions performed by human users [2].\n   - Use the `actor_user_uuid` parameter with the UUID of the specific user to further narrow the results [1].\n   - Example query:\n     ```\n     GET /v1/admin/audit-logs?event_type=le_chat.conversation.deleted&actor_type=HUMAN&actor_user_uuid=<USER_UUID>\n     ```\n\n3. **Default Number of Entries per Request**:\n   - By default, the API returns **20** entries per request [1].\n\n",
