{
  "answer_markdown": "To hand off your ongoing coding session from the terminal to the cloud (Vibe Code Web), use the `/teleport` command inside your active local session. This moves the session to a cloud sandbox while preserving its history and branch state, allowing you to continue working from the web interface [1].\n\n### What you give up by not using the editor surface:\n- **Local file system access**: The cloud session runs in an isolated sandbox and cannot directly access local files, services, or secrets outside the cloned repository [2].\n- **Direct shell or tool access**: Commands or tools requiring local machine-specific configurations (e.g., Docker, local databases, or unsupported runtimes) may not work [2].\n- **Real-time local editing**: You lose the ability to edit files directly in your local editor (e.g., VS Code) while the session runs in the cloud [2].\n- **Local environment dependencies**: Any dependencies or configurations tied to your local machine (e.g., environment variables, local ports) are not available in the cloud sandbox [2].",

  "citations": [
