  "answer_markdown": "When the **included monthly usage** on your Mistral plan runs out **without pay-as-you-go enabled**, your team's access to Mistral services (including the API, Vibe, and Studio) **stops until the next billing period begins** or an admin adjusts the settings [4]. This applies globally across the Organization, as the included usage is shared across all services [4] and Workspaces [3] (unless Workspace-specific limits are set, which are secondary to the Organization's plan limits [1][3][4]).\n\nIf the **Organization monthly spending limit** is reached instead, **API access for the entire Organization is suspended** until the next month begins or an admin increases the limit [1][2]. This is a separate cap from the included monthly usage and applies to both API and Vibe consumption [1][2]. Unlike the included usage exhaustion, this limit is enforced at the Organization level and does not depend on pay-as-you-go settings [1][2].\n\n### Key Differences:\n1. **Included monthly usage exhaustion (pay-as-you-go off)**:\n   - Access stops **only if pay-as-you-go is disabled** [4].\n   - Affects **all services (API, Vibe, Studio)** globally [4].\n   - Resumes automatically at the start of the next billing period [4].\n\n2. **Organization spending limit reached**:\n   - **API access is suspended** regardless of pay-as-you-go settings [1][2].\n   - Applies to **API and Vibe consumption** across the entire Organization [1][2].\n   - Resumes only after the next month begins or an admin adjusts the limit [1][2].\n\nFor Workspaces with their own spending limits, exceeding that limit **only suspends access for that specific Workspace**, while other Workspaces remain unaffected [3].",
